<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Csrank</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre><a cmd='#'>csrank</a>
csrank &lt;rank&gt; &lt;title&gt;
</pre>
<p>Example:
</p>
<pre>csrank 1 Newbie Power Master
</pre>
<p>A clan has 25 ranks, numbered 1 to 25, so that one clan's ranks can be compared 
with another's. Csrank lets the clan Master and the clan lords give those ranks 
titles of their own:
</p>
<ul><li><b>csrank</b> alone shows your clan's ranks and their titles. A new clan starts</li></ul>
<pre> with a set of military titles, from Private and Corporal up to the Generals, 
 with the top ranks blank.
</pre>
<ul><li><b>csrank &lt;rank&gt; &lt;title&gt;</b> gives rank &lt;rank&gt; a new title.</li></ul>
<p>To give a member a rank, use <a cmd='#'>Help Cpromote</a>. A rank without a title (blank) 
can't be given to anyone.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Cpromote</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Crank</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Clan Commands</a>
</pre>




</div>